  "prerequisite_scope": "Section 1B constructs metrizable Gleason–Yamabe and lifts its compact kernel to arbitrary locally compact Hausdorff groups at the exact general Haar and compact Peter–Weyl point-separation inputs. Section 1C constructs the closed solvable radical; Sections 1D–1E construct compact conjugation and the closed split rank-one subgroup for nonlinear groups and infinite centres. Theorem 3B.1 uses OA-FLOW-TG Sections 2–12 for all-orbit two-prescribed-gap tiling in original time, at its exact standard Borel and real-analysis inputs; the nonsingular measure-class passage is local Lemma 2.1. The represented-factor Connes assertion retains its original weak-measurable scope."
